    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="0960" n="950" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg950"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/7–2145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Political Adviser for Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 673</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frankfurt</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-21">July 21,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received August 6.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit a memorandum
                    by a member of my staff on observations on the situation in Munich, together
                    with an appendix on the views of leading Social Democrats in Munich. This
                    material throws some further light on potentialities for political action and
                    the balance of forces in Bavaria, though naturally no accurate <pb facs="0961"
                        n="951" xml:id="pg951"/> appraisal of popular support for the tendencies
                    discussed can be made at this time.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Murphy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d700-a1.xml" xpointer="d700-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
